			"Message": "fix(Project): Supply missing INativeWindowConfiguration fields in sandbox config and refresh doc diagrams\n\nAdd eight non-optional fields to Mountain's `ConstructSandboxConfiguration` JSON blob that VS Code's environment service layers access without null-checks: `perfMarks`, `loggers`, `colorScheme`, `mainPid`, `os` (release/hostname/arch), `dataFolderName`/`sharedDataFolderName` (defaulting to `.fiddee`), and `version`. Missing any of these causes a `TypeError` during extension host initialization and workbench service construction, crashing startup.\n\nIn Maintain, rewrite the Mermaid architecture diagram in README.md to document internal modules (Build CLI, Rhai scripting, Run logic), shell entrypoints (Debug/Release builds, SignBundle, BrotliPrebake), and build artifacts with color-coded classDefs. Also fix a literal tab character in PlistEdit.rs, replacing it with the escaped byte `\\t`.\n\nCocoon's Target artifacts are rebuilt and RouteManifest timestamp synchronized — no source-level changes, confirming the build pipeline consistency.\n\nThese changes prevent extension host startup crashes, improve developer documentation of the build system, and keep compiled artifacts aligned with source revisions.",
			"SHA": "b3e613bae60945dd1c50477d68489fc303e393ee"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T04:21:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⡿⠀⠀",
				26,
				15
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Integrate Mountain gRPC across Cocoon, wire custom editor and file watcher, overhaul documentation architecture diagrams\n\nWire live Mountain gRPC integration across four critical Cocoon service boundaries — command synchronization, extension registry, storage persistence, and command execution events — closing a longstanding integration gap. Implement the Mountain-side custom editor registry with proper cleanup on unregistration, route file watcher and PTY resize gRPC calls to real providers instead of no-op stubs, and add the extensions:activate handler to trigger programmatic extension activation via $activateByEvent.\n\nKey changes across components:\n- **Cocoon**: Wire MountainGRPCClientService for unregisterCommand synchronization, merge ILocalExtension manifests from Mountain into ExtensionRegistry, replace Memento storage stubs with Mountain-backed persistence, and subscribe to sky://commands/executed for onDidExecuteCommand. Purge stale Target/ build artifacts and simplify Command.ts by removing dynamic import indirection.\n- **Mountain**: Implement CustomEditorProvider registry, route watch_file and resize_terminal to real FSEvents/inotify and PTY SIGWINCH delivery, add extensions:activate handler, emit sky://commands/executed after command dispatch, add StorageWriteDebouncer with 100ms write coalescing, reduce command registration yield from 50ms to 20ms, and strip osascript subprocess from getCursorScreenPoint. Fix logsPath in ISandboxConfiguration to prevent extension host crash.\n- **Wind**: Remove mock Effect.sleep(10) from MountainSyncHelper and prune hundreds of stale generated upstream stubs and bridge shapes that no longer match current VS Code definitions.\n- **Common**: Add ExtensionsActivate IPC channel mapping to complete the Extensions channel group with an activation signal.\n- **Output**: Register five new channel bridges for VFS file changes, configuration updates, workspace folder changes, and lifecycle phase transitions, establishing a locked IPC contract between Output runtime and Wind's service layer.\n- **Documentation**: Redraw architecture diagrams across Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Mist, Mountain, Output, Rest, Sky, Vine, and Worker with detailed Mermaid subgraphs, subsystem hierarchies, and accurate IPC flow annotations to reflect current code structure.\n\nThese changes remove the last integration stubs between Cocoon and Mountain, optimize extension activation and command dispatch latency, and bring architectural documentation into alignment with the actual codebase.",
			"SHA": "08ff6e0f32047f1df417d94eea1e5f89157de321"
		}
